1
00:01:51,111 --> 00:01:55,111
You survived in the underworld by being quick to switch sides.

2
00:01:55,111 --> 00:01:58,111
And now you've chosen this crew as your next haven.

3
00:02:00,111 --> 00:02:06,111
Every organization that she's had something to do with in the past has been annihilated.

4
00:02:11,111 --> 00:02:13,111
Pistol!

5
00:02:21,111 --> 00:02:30,111
You have some very loyal friends, but you will never change, will you, Nico Robin?

6
00:02:31,111 --> 00:02:34,111
No! That's not true!

7
00:02:35,111 --> 00:02:36,111
Robin!

8
00:02:37,111 --> 00:02:39,111
I'm not who I am!

9
00:02:39,111 --> 00:02:40,111
Robin!

10
00:02:40,111 --> 00:02:41,111
Robin!

11
00:02:51,111 --> 00:02:54,111
Duel between rubber and ice. Luffy versus Aokiji.

12
00:02:54,111 --> 00:03:15,111
You bastard!

13
00:03:15,111 --> 00:03:22,111
Stop yelling. If you thaw her out carefully, she'll live.

14
00:03:22,111 --> 00:03:28,111
However, her body is extremely fragile in this state, so you'll need to handle her with care.

15
00:03:28,111 --> 00:03:30,111
If any part of her breaks, she'll die.

16
00:03:31,111 --> 00:03:35,111
For example, if I were to smash her apart like this...

17
00:03:36,111 --> 00:03:38,111
Robin!

18
00:03:39,111 --> 00:03:41,111
No!

19
00:03:42,111 --> 00:03:45,111
Stop!

20
00:03:52,111 --> 00:03:53,111
Uh?

21
00:03:53,111 --> 00:03:57,111
That was close!

22
00:03:57,111 --> 00:03:58,111
Oh, my!

23
00:03:58,111 --> 00:03:59,111
That was amazing, Usopp!

24
00:03:59,111 --> 00:04:00,111
What in the hell are you doing?

25
00:04:00,111 --> 00:04:01,111
Usopp!

26
00:04:01,111 --> 00:04:02,111
Chumper!

27
00:04:02,111 --> 00:04:03,111
Quick!

28
00:04:03,111 --> 00:04:04,111
Take Robin and run back to the ship!

29
00:04:04,111 --> 00:04:05,111
Throw her out and keep her safe!

30
00:04:05,111 --> 00:04:06,111
Right!

31
00:04:06,111 --> 00:04:07,111
You got it, Captain!

32
00:04:07,111 --> 00:04:08,111
Hurry!

33
00:04:08,111 --> 00:04:09,111
Be gentle, okay?

34
00:04:09,111 --> 00:04:10,111
It's cold!

35
00:04:10,111 --> 00:04:11,111
I know, but Robin's even colder, genius!

36
00:04:11,111 --> 00:04:16,111
Don't bother. The world would be a much better place without that woman in...

37
00:04:16,111 --> 00:04:23,111
Not to split hairs, but a pirate crew pretty much consists of people just like that.

38
00:04:23,111 --> 00:04:30,111
You got that right, lady. Now, if you don't mind, kindly step aside.

39
00:04:30,111 --> 00:04:33,111
Nami! You're not gonna mess with this crew!

40
00:04:33,111 --> 00:04:36,111
Wait! Nobody attack him!

41
00:04:36,111 --> 00:04:37,111
Huh?

42
00:04:37,111 --> 00:04:38,111
Huh?

43
00:04:38,111 --> 00:04:39,111
Stay back and don't interfere. I'm gonna fight him one-on-one.

44
00:04:39,111 --> 00:04:40,111
What do you want?

45
00:04:40,111 --> 00:04:41,111
What do you want to do, isn't it?

46
00:04:41,111 --> 00:04:42,111
Oh, oh, I'm gonna fight him!

47
00:04:42,111 --> 00:04:43,111
No!

48
00:04:43,111 --> 00:04:44,111
I'm gonna fight him!

49
00:04:44,111 --> 00:04:45,111
Oh, oh, oh, oh!

50
00:04:45,111 --> 00:04:46,111
Look!

51
00:04:46,111 --> 00:04:47,111
It's just a pirate crew.

52
00:04:47,111 --> 00:04:48,111
You got that right, lady.

53
00:04:48,111 --> 00:04:49,111
Now, if you don't mind, kindly step aside.

54
00:04:49,111 --> 00:04:50,111
Ah!

55
00:04:50,111 --> 00:04:51,111
Nami!

56
00:04:51,111 --> 00:04:52,111
You're not gonna mess with this crew!

57
00:04:52,111 --> 00:04:54,111
Wait! Nobody attack him!

58
00:04:54,111 --> 00:04:55,111
Huh?

59
00:04:57,111 --> 00:04:59,111
Stay back and don't interfere!

60
00:04:59,111 --> 00:05:00,111
I'm gonna fight him one-on-one!

61
00:05:01,111 --> 00:05:02,111
What do you want to do?

62
00:05:02,111 --> 00:05:04,111
What do you want to do?

63
00:05:04,111 --> 00:05:06,731
What do you say?

64
00:05:07,051 --> 00:05:09,451
The two of us can settle this on our own.

65
00:05:10,291 --> 00:05:11,411
Fine by me.

66
00:05:11,711 --> 00:05:14,191
But since I don't have a ship to take you back,

67
00:05:14,471 --> 00:05:16,251
then I'll just have to kill you.

68
00:05:20,231 --> 00:05:22,931
She can't breathe like this, can she?

69
00:05:23,151 --> 00:05:25,291
I think she's in a state of suspended animation.

70
00:05:25,551 --> 00:05:27,651
Doesn't that mean she'll die if we don't do something?

71
00:05:27,911 --> 00:05:29,911
If we warm her up too quickly, she'll shatter.

72
00:05:30,131 --> 00:05:33,071
We have to restore her body temperature from the inside out.

73
00:05:34,111 --> 00:05:36,751
Are you sure that this is really going to work?

74
00:05:37,511 --> 00:05:40,231
I don't know, but it's the only thing I...

75
00:05:40,231 --> 00:05:41,691
Whoa, wait a minute. You don't know?

76
00:05:41,891 --> 00:05:43,811
This is Robin's life we're talking about here.

77
00:05:44,331 --> 00:05:46,771
I know, but I've never treated someone

78
00:05:46,771 --> 00:05:48,851
whose entire body was frozen before.

79
00:05:49,171 --> 00:05:51,611
I know that Aokiji said she was still alive,

80
00:05:52,131 --> 00:05:54,491
but I just don't see how that could be possible.

81
00:05:54,511 --> 00:05:55,551
Don't give me that crap.

82
00:05:55,891 --> 00:05:57,291
If you can't do anything to save her,

83
00:05:57,351 --> 00:05:58,671
then no one in the whole world can.

84
00:05:58,771 --> 00:05:59,871
You understand me?

85
00:06:00,011 --> 00:06:02,471
You are the doctor of the straw hat pirates, got it?

86
00:06:02,471 --> 00:06:05,311
I know, okay? Just shut up and stop yelling at me!

87
00:06:22,991 --> 00:06:23,551
Chopper!

88
00:06:23,551 --> 00:06:31,211
What's going on? Why are just the three of you here?

89
00:06:31,291 --> 00:06:31,911
Where's Luffy?

90
00:06:32,151 --> 00:06:33,491
There's no time to explain.

91
00:06:33,691 --> 00:06:35,471
We need to go back right away.

92
00:06:35,731 --> 00:06:37,931
Help us do something about this frozen arm and leg.

93
00:06:37,951 --> 00:06:38,671
Oh, right.

94
00:06:38,991 --> 00:06:39,431
We...

95
00:06:39,431 --> 00:06:41,891
We need to douse every part of your body

96
00:06:41,891 --> 00:06:43,091
that's frozen in water.

97
00:06:43,651 --> 00:06:45,791
But we're using the shower room for Robin.

98
00:06:46,051 --> 00:06:47,531
How is Robin? Is she okay?

99
00:06:47,771 --> 00:06:49,731
Uh, it's too early to tell.

100
00:06:49,731 --> 00:06:51,651
What are you doing?

101
00:06:53,711 --> 00:06:55,151
Will this do chopper?

102
00:06:58,591 --> 00:07:00,431
Yes. Once the ice begins to melt,

103
00:07:00,551 --> 00:07:01,991
start rubbing the affected areas

104
00:07:01,991 --> 00:07:03,891
and then come up to the ship right away.

105
00:07:04,811 --> 00:07:07,091
Nami, come aboard and help us treat Robin.

106
00:07:07,351 --> 00:07:07,731
Right.

107
00:07:07,731 --> 00:07:13,551
What the...

108
00:07:13,551 --> 00:07:14,651
Why are you guys here?

109
00:07:14,991 --> 00:07:15,871
What happened?

110
00:07:16,111 --> 00:07:16,791
Where's Luffy?

111
00:07:18,211 --> 00:07:20,211
Fighting out Kiji one-on-one.

112
00:07:20,491 --> 00:07:21,471
One-on-one?

113
00:07:21,651 --> 00:07:22,911
You mean you left Luffy there

114
00:07:22,911 --> 00:07:24,291
to face him all by himself?

115
00:07:25,871 --> 00:07:27,491
Those were the captain's orders.

116
00:07:27,871 --> 00:07:28,731
Are you crazy?

117
00:07:28,891 --> 00:07:30,731
Can't you tell when an order is unreasonable?

118
00:07:31,131 --> 00:07:33,151
I can't believe you would be so cold-hearted

119
00:07:33,151 --> 00:07:34,391
as to just leave a head.

120
00:07:34,391 --> 00:07:35,751
It was a duel.

121
00:07:35,871 --> 00:07:37,011
Can't you understand that?

122
00:07:37,051 --> 00:07:37,851
It's what he wanted.

123
00:07:38,051 --> 00:07:39,211
Stop it, both of you.

124
00:07:39,291 --> 00:07:40,331
This isn't the time.

125
00:07:42,031 --> 00:07:45,211
Right now, we need to stay focused, okay?

126
00:07:46,531 --> 00:07:49,451
Whether this decision was one of his passing whims or not,

127
00:07:49,491 --> 00:07:50,251
it doesn't matter.

128
00:07:50,571 --> 00:07:51,311
Whatever happens,

129
00:07:51,391 --> 00:07:53,051
we have to be ready to deal with it.

130
00:07:53,111 --> 00:07:53,511
Understand?

131
00:07:53,511 --> 00:08:05,431
You really are an odd one, aren't you?

132
00:08:05,431 --> 00:08:35,411
You really are an odd one, aren't you?

133
00:08:35,411 --> 00:08:48,531
Now it's ice time.

134
00:09:05,411 --> 00:09:15,211
What do you say?

135
00:09:15,211 --> 00:09:17,711
The two of us can settle this on our own.

136
00:09:22,711 --> 00:09:24,031
Oh, man.

137
00:09:24,331 --> 00:09:25,731
You tricked me.

138
00:09:26,391 --> 00:09:29,331
The moment I agreed to fight you one-on-one,

139
00:09:29,471 --> 00:09:32,211
I settled on defeating you and you alone.

140
00:09:32,491 --> 00:09:34,311
But that was your plan, wasn't it?

141
00:09:34,311 --> 00:09:36,511
If I were to attack your crew now,

142
00:09:36,751 --> 00:09:38,431
I'd be the bad guy here.

143
00:09:38,891 --> 00:09:40,551
Isn't that right, Captain?

144
00:09:41,951 --> 00:09:46,471
Or maybe you actually thought you could beat me.

145
00:09:51,351 --> 00:09:53,851
Let me give you a piece of advice.

146
00:09:54,711 --> 00:09:56,951
Keep a close eye on Nico Robin.

147
00:09:57,771 --> 00:10:01,191
Eventually, she'll grow to be more than you can handle.

148
00:10:04,311 --> 00:10:08,291
The nature of the violent fate she was born into

149
00:10:08,291 --> 00:10:11,051
will be a greater danger than you can imagine.

150
00:10:11,651 --> 00:10:15,731
More of a burden than you could ever hope to bear.

151
00:10:19,471 --> 00:10:22,931
That's what it means to have that woman as part of your crew.

152
00:10:24,211 --> 00:10:25,771
You have been warned,

153
00:10:25,771 --> 00:10:28,531
Mr. Monkey D.

154
00:10:28,531 --> 00:10:29,171
Mr. Monkey D. Luffy.

155
00:10:34,971 --> 00:10:39,451
It would be easy to break you and kill you right here and now.

156
00:10:40,051 --> 00:10:41,791
But I have a debt to honor.

157
00:10:41,791 --> 00:10:50,951
Consider us even for you taking care of Crocodile.

158
00:10:52,091 --> 00:10:52,791
As well as...

159
00:10:54,551 --> 00:10:57,431
Well, never mind.

160
00:10:57,811 --> 00:10:59,251
Something to do with Smoker.

161
00:10:59,931 --> 00:11:00,711
See ya.

162
00:11:00,711 --> 00:11:08,031
There he is!

163
00:11:08,691 --> 00:11:09,251
Luffy!

164
00:11:10,391 --> 00:11:12,071
He's still in one piece!

165
00:11:12,571 --> 00:11:13,751
That's good news!

166
00:11:14,251 --> 00:11:14,931
I'll carry him!

167
00:11:15,331 --> 00:11:16,411
Let's get him to the ship!

168
00:11:16,671 --> 00:11:18,171
Stop saying what I'm saying!

169
00:11:18,171 --> 00:11:30,731
If they follow their log pose from this island,

170
00:11:30,731 --> 00:11:33,111
their next destination is...

171
00:11:33,111 --> 00:11:35,831
It's Water 7.

172
00:11:36,471 --> 00:11:38,131
The City of Water, huh?

173
00:11:38,511 --> 00:11:39,791
Oh, my, my, my.

174
00:11:39,911 --> 00:11:41,111
Would you look at that?

175
00:11:41,651 --> 00:11:44,871
They're getting really close to our headquarters, aren't they?

176
00:11:44,871 --> 00:12:04,071
I'm saying...

177
00:12:05,171 --> 00:12:06,011
I'm saying...

178
00:12:08,791 --> 00:12:12,611
What do you want?

179
00:12:12,611 --> 00:12:28,771
Both... of their hearts... are beating!

180
00:12:29,571 --> 00:12:29,971
Yeah!

181
00:12:31,411 --> 00:12:32,091
Snoopy!

182
00:12:32,811 --> 00:12:33,331
Norman!

183
00:12:33,811 --> 00:12:35,271
No, you can't go in yet!

184
00:12:35,311 --> 00:12:36,891
I don't want them disturbed, understand?

185
00:12:37,551 --> 00:12:40,731
Hey, Dr. Chopper, how about I make them some food?

186
00:12:40,731 --> 00:12:45,671
Calling me doctor won't make me feel happy or anything, you stupid jerk!

187
00:12:45,931 --> 00:12:49,091
But I suppose some warm drinks would be nice for when they wake up.

188
00:12:49,351 --> 00:12:51,011
I'll carry them into the lounge later.

189
00:12:51,471 --> 00:12:52,271
Aye, aye, sir!

190
00:12:53,111 --> 00:12:54,951
Hey, Nami, should we set sail?

191
00:12:55,351 --> 00:12:56,251
No, not yet.

192
00:12:56,571 --> 00:12:58,111
Not while the captain's out of commission.

193
00:12:58,451 --> 00:13:01,151
The lock pose has our new heading, but let's rest here for the day.

194
00:13:05,911 --> 00:13:07,051
What's wrong, Usopp?

195
00:13:07,051 --> 00:13:07,911
You look beat.

196
00:13:07,911 --> 00:13:11,171
Are there gonna be more guys like him?

197
00:13:11,391 --> 00:13:13,731
Coming after us everywhere we go?

198
00:13:15,891 --> 00:13:17,211
This is crazy.

199
00:13:17,631 --> 00:13:19,951
I don't know how much more of it I can take.

200
00:13:20,811 --> 00:13:22,231
Get some sleep, idiot.

201
00:13:22,531 --> 00:13:24,071
You're just exhausted, okay?

202
00:13:24,071 --> 00:13:24,191
Okay.

203
00:13:24,191 --> 00:13:38,751
Go, go, go, go, go.

204
00:13:38,751 --> 00:14:02,971
In order for Luffy and Robin to get some rest and recover, the Going Mary remained anchored off the uninhabited island for four days.

205
00:14:02,971 --> 00:14:05,031
After that, we set sail.

206
00:14:05,571 --> 00:14:08,531
Today marks the third morning since we resumed our voyage.

207
00:14:08,751 --> 00:14:13,751
The weather is clear and sunny, mostly spring, with occasional bouts of summer.

208
00:14:18,751 --> 00:14:20,751
It's beautiful!

209
00:14:20,751 --> 00:14:23,751
Nami, look!

210
00:14:26,751 --> 00:14:30,751
I made this potato pie especially for you, mademoiselle.

211
00:14:30,751 --> 00:14:32,751
I hope you enjoy it.

212
00:14:32,751 --> 00:14:35,751
Mmm, delicious!

213
00:14:35,751 --> 00:14:37,751
That makes me so happy!

214
00:14:37,751 --> 00:14:39,751
Hey, keep it down, jerk!

215
00:14:39,751 --> 00:14:41,751
Some people are trying to sleep around here!

216
00:14:41,751 --> 00:14:43,751
Sorry about that, cactus head.

217
00:14:43,751 --> 00:14:44,751
My most sincere apology.

218
00:14:44,751 --> 00:14:46,751
What, you cigarette snorkeling dartboard?

219
00:14:46,751 --> 00:14:47,751
Huh?

220
00:14:47,751 --> 00:14:49,751
What did you call me?

221
00:14:49,751 --> 00:14:50,751
Dartboard.

222
00:14:50,751 --> 00:14:51,751
Dartboard eyebrows.

223
00:14:51,751 --> 00:14:52,751
What?

224
00:14:52,751 --> 00:14:53,751
What?

225
00:14:53,751 --> 00:14:54,751
Lou!

226
00:14:54,751 --> 00:14:55,751
Bee!

227
00:14:55,751 --> 00:14:56,751
Lou!

228
00:14:56,751 --> 00:14:57,751
Bee!

229
00:14:57,751 --> 00:14:58,751
Lou!

230
00:14:58,751 --> 00:14:59,751
Bee!

231
00:14:59,751 --> 00:15:00,751
Lou!

232
00:15:00,751 --> 00:15:01,751
Bee!

233
00:15:01,751 --> 00:15:02,751
Lou!

234
00:15:02,751 --> 00:15:03,751
Bee!

235
00:15:03,751 --> 00:15:04,751
Bee!

236
00:15:04,751 --> 00:15:05,751
Bee!

237
00:15:05,751 --> 00:15:06,751
Woo!

238
00:15:06,751 --> 00:15:07,751
We've been waiting for this!

239
00:15:07,751 --> 00:15:08,751
Lou!

240
00:15:08,751 --> 00:15:09,751
Bee!

241
00:15:09,751 --> 00:15:10,751
Ha-ha!

242
00:15:11,751 --> 00:15:14,751
This is me frozen!

243
00:15:14,751 --> 00:15:29,751
I can't believe this is how he behaves after almost freezing to death!

244
00:15:29,751 --> 00:15:31,751
What do you think?

245
00:15:31,751 --> 00:15:32,751
You nailed it!

246
00:15:32,751 --> 00:15:34,751
That's exactly what you looked like!

247
00:15:34,751 --> 00:15:37,751
Make sure you clean all that up, Luffy!

248
00:15:37,751 --> 00:15:38,751
Kay!

249
00:15:38,751 --> 00:15:39,751
Hey, Nami, is that food?

250
00:15:39,751 --> 00:15:40,751
What are you eating?

251
00:15:40,751 --> 00:15:42,751
Some potato pie-ee!

252
00:15:42,751 --> 00:15:44,751
Potatoes, huh?

253
00:15:44,751 --> 00:15:45,751
I love potatoes!

254
00:15:45,751 --> 00:15:46,751
Sanji, make me some!

255
00:15:46,751 --> 00:15:50,751
Just how many hours a day do you have to lie around and sleep anyway?

256
00:15:50,751 --> 00:15:51,751
That's none of your business!

257
00:15:51,751 --> 00:15:52,751
I'll sleep as long as I like!

258
00:15:52,751 --> 00:15:53,751
Wanna fight about it?

259
00:15:53,751 --> 00:15:55,751
Okay, you two, enough!

260
00:15:55,751 --> 00:15:58,751
Sanji, our captain has requested some of your potato pie-ee!

261
00:15:58,751 --> 00:15:59,751
You got it, Nami!

262
00:15:59,751 --> 00:16:00,751
Sanji!

263
00:16:00,751 --> 00:16:01,751
Potatoes!

264
00:16:01,751 --> 00:16:06,751
You're still recuperating, but that hasn't slowed down your appetite in the slightest, has it?

265
00:16:12,751 --> 00:16:13,751
So this is pie, huh?

266
00:16:13,751 --> 00:16:14,751
Good stuff!

267
00:16:14,751 --> 00:16:16,751
Why is it called that?

268
00:16:16,751 --> 00:16:20,751
Because the meat is taken from the tail of the giant beast pie-ee!

269
00:16:20,751 --> 00:16:22,751
I should know, I was the one who killed it!

270
00:16:22,751 --> 00:16:24,751
It was over a hundred meters long!

271
00:16:24,751 --> 00:16:25,751
Whoa!

272
00:16:25,751 --> 00:16:26,751
A hundred meters?

273
00:16:26,751 --> 00:16:27,751
That's amazing, Uzo!

274
00:16:27,751 --> 00:16:29,751
And I did it all before breakfast!

275
